# Fixtures for the development bench. Tracked, and not a file an operator edits.
#
# `172.28.0.20`, `alice`, `bob` are the same on every bench that has ever run.
# They are not decisions anyone makes, so they do not belong in .env -- which is
# gitignored and per-operator, and was the only reason these were ever in front
# of someone deploying a real realm. deploy/GLOSSARY.md @ fixture (deployment).
#
# Compose reads this because deploy/Makefile exports
# COMPOSE_ENV_FILES = bench.env,.env -- in that order, because the last file
# wins and the operator's own .env must be the one that does. Scripts that read
# these as shell source the pair in the same order.
#
# Nothing here is a secret and nothing here is inert-if-wrong: a value that
# disagrees with the config set breaks the bench loudly. Overriding one is a
# line in .env, or a variable in the environment, which beats both files.

# --- The seeded demo directory: scripts/bench/seed-demo.sh ------------------

# The first person. Must be the real `oid` from the token, or every login is a
# 403 -- this is the one value a live-tenant bench has to change. Re-running the
# seed rewrites the stored identity, so changing it is safe.
SEED_USER_OID=33334444-dddd-5555-eeee-6666ffff7777
SEED_USER_NAME=alice

# The second person and the service account exist only for the delegation path.
# The oids are make_fixtures.py's, which is what joins them to a token; no token
# is ever issued for the service account -- it never signs in at a browser,
# which is the whole reason it needs a delegate -- so its id only has to be
# distinct.
SEED_OTHER_NAME=bob
SEED_OTHER_OID=44445555-eeee-6666-ffff-7777aaaa8888
SEED_SERVICE_NAME=svc-builder
SEED_SERVICE_OID=55556666-ffff-7777-aaaa-8888bbbb9999

# Deliberately not here: SEED_ADMISSION_GROUP and SEED_GRANT_GROUP. The seed
# defaults both, and the broker finds either group by the marker the seed stamps
# rather than by its name, so a bench that wants other names sets them in its own
# environment. SEED_DELEGATE_GROUP is derived from SEED_SERVICE_NAME by the seed
# rather than stated here: it is a function of a fixture, not one.

# --- The mock IdP overlay: `make up MOCKIDP=1` ------------------------------

# compose.mockidp.yaml has no default for this and refuses to start without it:
# the `iss` the broker accepts is built from a tenant id, so the mock must be
# told the one the source file states. This is what configs/idp_entra.toml.example
# ships, and scripts/compose/check-compose-env.py holds the pair together.
MOCK_IDP_TENANT_ID=aaaabbbb-0000-cccc-1111-dddd2222eeee

# --- The example file server: `make up NAS=1` -------------------------------

# SET NAS_HOSTNAME ONCE, BEFORE THE FIRST JOIN -- it becomes the member's
# NetBIOS name and its machine account in the durable m1-samba volume, and
# nothing refuses to start on a mismatch. compose.nas.yaml @ nas1 has the rest.
NAS_HOSTNAME=nas1
NAS_IPV4=172.28.0.20
